VALUES (440097192101016, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Applied Physics requires a student to choose an appropriate procedure for a task involving unit within the unit Units, Dimensions and Measurements. Explain how Definition of unit applies, set out the main steps or reasoning, and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Applied Physics requires a student to justify a design choice using the rule associated with Inertia, rather than confusing it with a related concept. Explain how Inertia applies, set out the main steps or reasoning, and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Applied Physics requires a student to choose an appropriate procedure for a task involving systems of units- CGS within the unit Units, Dimensions and Measurements. Explain how systems of units- CGS applies, set out the main steps or reasoning, and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Applied Physics requires a student to choose an appropriate procedure for a task involving MKS and SI within the unit Units, Dimensions and Measurements. Explain how MKS and SI applies, set out the main steps or reasoning, and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Definition of unit is addressed within the syllabus unit “Units, Dimensions and Measurements”. A complete answer should define the term precisely, explain its role in the unit, identify its main inputs or components, and describe how it is applied or evaluated in a realistic task. Relate it to nearby syllabus concepts such as Fundamental and Derived units, systems of units- CGS, MKS and SI, introduction to accuracy, precision and errors, then give a specific example and state a limitation or verification step.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are Fundamental and Derived units; systems of units- CGS; MKS and SI; introduction to accuracy. Relate each element to the purpose of Definition of unit, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Applied Physics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Newton''s first law states that an object remains at rest or in uniform straight-line motion unless acted on by a non-zero resultant external force. Inertia is the resistance to a change in motion, and mass measures this property.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are Newton''s first law of motion; momentum; Newton’s second law of motion; conservation of momentum. Relate each element to the purpose of Inertia, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Applied Physics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** systems of units- CGS is addressed within the syllabus unit “Units, Dimensions and Measurements”. A complete answer should define the term precisely, explain its role in the unit, identify its main inputs or components, and describe how it is applied or evaluated in a realistic task. Relate it to nearby syllabus concepts such as Definition of unit, Fundamental and Derived units, MKS and SI, introduction to accuracy, precision and errors, then give a specific example and state a limitation or verification step.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are Definition of unit; Fundamental and Derived units; MKS and SI; introduction to accuracy. Relate each element to the purpose of systems of units- CGS, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Applied Physics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** MKS and SI is addressed within the syllabus unit “Units, Dimensions and Measurements”. A complete answer should define the term precisely, explain its role in the unit, identify its main inputs or components, and describe how it is applied or evaluated in a realistic task. Relate it to nearby syllabus concepts such as Definition of unit, Fundamental and Derived units, systems of units- CGS, introduction to accuracy, precision and errors, then give a specific example and state a limitation or verification step.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are Definition of unit; Fundamental and Derived units; systems of units- CGS; introduction to accuracy. Relate each element to the purpose of MKS and SI, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Applied Physics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

