VALUES (4400971921010136, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Inertia in Applied Physics. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Stress & strain along with their types in Applied Physics. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Current electricity: current in Applied Physics. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Fundamental and Derived units in Applied Physics. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or decision, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Newton''s first law states that an object remains at rest or in uniform straight-line motion unless acted on by a non-zero resultant external force. Inertia is the resistance to a change in motion, and mass measures this property.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are Newton''s first law of motion; momentum; Newton’s second law of motion; conservation of momentum. Relate each element to the purpose of Inertia, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Applied Physics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Stress & strain along with their types is addressed within the syllabus unit “Properties of Matter”. A complete answer should define the term precisely, explain its role in the unit, identify its main inputs or components, and describe how it is applied or evaluated in a realistic task. Relate it to nearby syllabus concepts such as Hooke''s law and modulus of elasticity-Young, bulk and modulus of rigidity, Viscosity, newton''s law of viscosity, types of flows, then give a specific example and state a limitation or verification step.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are Hooke''s law and modulus of elasticity-Young; bulk and modulus of rigidity; Viscosity; newton''s law of viscosity. Relate each element to the purpose of Stress & strain along with their types, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Applied Physics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Current electricity: current is addressed within the syllabus unit “Electro-Magnetism”. A complete answer should define the term precisely, explain its role in the unit, identify its main inputs or components, and describe how it is applied or evaluated in a realistic task. Relate it to nearby syllabus concepts such as EMF and Ohm''s law, resistance, series and parallel, Magnetism: Magnetic field and properties, electro-magnetic induction-self-inductance and mutual inductance, then give a specific example and state a limitation or verification step.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are EMF and Ohm''s law; resistance; series and parallel; Magnetism: Magnetic field and properties. Relate each element to the purpose of Current electricity: current, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Applied Physics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A unit provides a defined standard for expressing a measured physical quantity. Fundamental units are independent standards, while derived units are combinations of them; consistent units are essential before comparing or calculating quantities.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are Definition of unit; systems of units- CGS; MKS and SI; introduction to accuracy. Relate each element to the purpose of Fundamental and Derived units, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Applied Physics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

