VALUES (440009552103011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Types of semiconductors. in the context of Diode characteristics and its applications. Define it and describe its key principles or steps, with one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain PNP and NPN transistors in the context of Transistor characteristics and applications. Define it and describe its key principles or steps, with one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain P-N junction diode formation and characteristics. in the context of Diode characteristics and its applications. Define it and describe its key principles or steps, with one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Applications - Diode as rectifier in the context of Diode characteristics and its applications. Define it and describe its key principles or steps, with one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A PN-junction diode is formed by joining p-type and n-type semiconductor regions. Its depletion region and potential barrier explain its direction-dependent current; forward bias reduces the barrier and reverse bias increases it.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are P-N junction diode formation and characteristics.; Applications - Diode as rectifier; half wave; full wave and bridge rectifier. Relate each element to the purpose of Types of semiconductors., and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Basic Electronics task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is 