orking (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are Built-in-function- Math function; console & standard i/o function; user defined function; recursion. Relate each element to the purpose of Definition of function, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Computer Programming task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Definition of structure is addressed within the syllabus unit “Structure & Union”. A complete answer should define the term precisely, explain its role in the unit, identify its main inputs or components, and describe how it is applied or evaluated in a realistic task. Relate it to nearby syllabus concepts such as need of structure, declaration of structure, array within structure, structure within structure, structure and union difference, then give a specific example and state a limitation or verification step.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are need of structure; declaration of structure; array within structure; structure within structure. Relate each element to the purpose of Definition of structure, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Computer Programming task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

