elf-improvement enables them to secure a bright future for themselves. They will learn 6 powerful thought- processes that can develop their intellectual; physical; emotional; and spiritual quotients.. Relate each element to the purpose of Students learn how self-improvement enables them to secure a bright future for themselve, and state any conditions or assumptions that affect the result.\n\n**Application and example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a realistic Integrated Personality Development Course-I task. Identify the requirement, select the relevant procedure or component, and explain the expected result instead of only listing terminology.\n\n**Check and conclusion (1 mark):** Verify the outcome against the stated requirement; mention a meaningful limitation, error source or design trade-off. End by stating why the concept is suitable for the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; accurate principles or steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Students will undergo a study of how habits work is addressed within the syllabus unit “Remaking Yourself Power of Habit”. A complete answer should define the term precisely, explain its role in the unit, identify its main inputs or components, and describe how it is applied or evaluated in a realistic task. Relate it to nearby syllabus concepts such as the habits of successful professionals, and the practical techniques that can be used to develop good habits in their life., Remaking Yourself Power of Habit, then give a specific example and state a limitation or verification step.\n\n**Principles or working (3 marks):** Explain the main elements in a logical order. In this syllabus unit, the closely related areas are the habits of successful professionals; and the practical techniques that can be used to develop good habits in their life.; Remaking Yourself Power of Habit. Relate each element to the purpose of Students w